                "y": -125,
                "z": 2
            },
            {
                "drawing_id": "608d77a5-ba22-448b-97b6-57cf0e0726d1",
                "locked": false,
                "rotation": 0,
                "svg": "<svg width=\"542\" height=\"264\"><text font-family=\"TypeWriter\" font-size=\"10.0\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000000\" fill-opacity=\"1.0\">1. Configure the correct IP address/subnet mask on each PC.\n    Set the gateway address as the LAST USABLE address of the sunet.\n\n2. Make three connection between R1 and SW1.\n    Configure on interface on R1 for each VLAN.\n    Make sure the IP addresses are the gateway address you configure on the PCs.\n\n3. Configure SW1 's interfaces in the proper VLANS.\n    Remember the interface that connect to R1.\n    Name th VLANs (Engineering, HR, Sales).\n\n4. Ping between the PCs to check connectivity.\n    Send a broadcast ping from a PC (pingg the subnet broadcast address). and see\n   with PCs devices receive the broadcast \n\n</text></svg>",
                "x": -873,
                "y": 241,
                "z": 2
            },
